<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Austrian Delagoa Bay</h1><p class="st-meta">1777 CE – 1781 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Habsburg monarchy's only African colony, a brief trading venture on Delagoa Bay led by the adventurer William Bolts.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-bolts">William Bolts</a>, a former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> servant, persuaded the Austrian government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> to back a trading venture to the East under the imperial flag. In 1777 he landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delagoa-bay">Delagoa Bay</a> and signed agreements with local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsonga-people">Tsonga</a> rulers, including the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tembe-kingdom">Tembe Kingdom</a>, to establish trading posts.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Austrian posts, run by agents of Bolts's company and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-asiatic-company-of-trieste">Imperial Asiatic Company of Trieste</a>, traded cloth and metal goods for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>. The settlement was tiny and dependent on the goodwill of local rulers, and it was meant to link Austrian trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Portugal, which claimed the bay, sent a naval force in 1781 that expelled the Austrians and built a fort. Bolts's company soon failed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> made no further colonial attempts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1777 CE – 1781 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden